export const body = "<div class=\"source-table\"><table><tbody><tr><td><div class=\"source-table\"><table><tbody><tr><td><p>Born in 1980, <em>Pac-Man</em> quickly exploded into a cultural phenomenon, and the eponymous player avatar soon became the series mascot. The immediate infatuation translated into dozens of titles across arcade machines, home consoles, and mobile devices—with the latest installment, <em>Pac-Man 99</em>, released as early as April 2021.</p>\n<p>In this short article, we'll talk about the origin of video game's number one eating enthusiast: how he got his name and how he got his look.</p></td><td><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/cookies-inline/686138560b5676e141a0.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/cookies-inline/686138560b5676e141a0.webp\" width=\"750\" height=\"750\" style=\"--source-width:248px\" alt=\"Illustration 1\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/cookies-inline/73a0887b435d7c0b2463.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/cookies-inline/73a0887b435d7c0b2463.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"493\" style=\"--source-width:297px\" alt=\"Illustration 2\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td><td><p>During the 1970s, arcade games mostly centered around themes of war or sports, appealing more to men than to women. Unsatisfied with the status quo, a young designer aspired to create a family-friendly game, something women and couples could enjoy at the arcades. The game would be non-violent and feature cute characters. Eventually, he arrived at a gameplay loop that centered around eating. <em>Pac-Man</em> was conceived.</p>\n<p>The tongue in cheek nature of <em>Pac-Man</em> offered the much-needed levity to the video game landscape of the arcade era, and thus it was well-received, finding success across Japan. To capitalize on their new success, the developer went on to distribute the game internationally. And this is where the name came from.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Originally, the game was called <em>Pakkuman</em>, mimicking the Japanese term for chomping food “paku paku taberu.\" But when the localization team in the U.S. realized the translated name was going to be \"Puck-Man,\" they promptly suggested changing it to Pac-Man. <sub>(Because people who speak English have an irresistible itch to add an F to any words that contain U, C, K.)</sub></p>\n<p>When asked about the character design, the designer either said he was inspired by the shape of a pizza with a slice missing he once had for lunch, or Pac-Man was the result of him rounding out the Japanese word for the mouth: “kuchi” (口).The core value of Pac-Man</p>\n<p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/cookies-inline/1ed378eb9137bf58de96.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/cookies-inline/1ed378eb9137bf58de96.webp\" width=\"1080\" height=\"705\" style=\"--source-width:297px\" alt=\"Illustration 3\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td><td><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/cookies-inline/068a2dfe363fcf801601.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/cookies-inline/068a2dfe363fcf801601.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" style=\"--source-width:248px\" alt=\"Illustration 4\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p>\n<p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/cookies-inline/7813ea5e36e82e1bcfbc.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/cookies-inline/7813ea5e36e82e1bcfbc.webp\" width=\"1080\" height=\"434\" style=\"--source-width:248px\" alt=\"Illustration 5\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/cookies-inline/8436c440271bcd8eb7c7.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/cookies-inline/8436c440271bcd8eb7c7.webp\" width=\"620\" height=\"372\" style=\"--source-width:297px\" alt=\"Illustration 6\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td><td><p>As for color, we have a theory as to why Pac-Man is yellow (barring the semblance to pizza). So, the maze is <strong>pitch black</strong>, its walls outlined in <strong>dark blue</strong>, which means any moving entity has to dress a bright color to contrast against the environment. This is true for all four ghosts in the game. And Mr. Chompy, being the player character, has the privilege to wear the brightest color of all, which is <strong>yellow</strong>.</p>\n<p>Of course, we don't know whether or not the designer had this in mind when he chose the dress code for his cast of characters. But it ended up working in the game's favor, so we think it's worth pointing out.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Despite a history spanning more than four decades, Pac-Man has barely seen any significant design changes over the years. In commercial material, the hungry mascot may have an additional pair of arms, a pair of legs with boots on, and an overly expressive face, but during gameplay, he will always be a chompy yellow dot, unceasingly eating his way out of an endless maze.</p></td><td><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/cookies-inline/d153b97f4ac8246f708e.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/cookies-inline/d153b97f4ac8246f708e.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"598\" style=\"--source-width:248px\" alt=\"Illustration 7\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></td></tr></tbody></table></div>";
